      "id": "macbeth/sceneV_20.8/p@144848",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MACDUFF.\nHail, King, for so thou art. Behold, where stands\nTh’ usurper’s cursed head: the time is free.\nI see thee compass’d with thy kingdom’s pearl,\nThat speak my salutation in their minds;\nWhose voices I desire aloud with mine,—\nHail, King of Scotland!",
